Z||000000||Cooter||04-07-2000||11:45 PM||||Does anybody know something about them? I bought one for my 3.4 conversion hoping it would be more quiet than the flowmasters on my Suburban. After looking at the muffler, it looks like it could be pretty loud. Even though it is a "turbo" style muffler, you can see through it, so I cant imagine that it will be too quite. Any insight would be appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-08-2000||01:15 PM||||I actually live a couple miles from the Flowtech factory.  I believe they're fully welded.  They used to say that you could toss a grenade in one end, and it would spit it out the other.  I've heard the sound is comparable to flowmaster(which are loud.) If it's a two-chamber, it's going to pretty loud.  3 chambers are fairly quiet.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||04-08-2000||04:42 PM||||That's what I was afraid of. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||04-08-2000||07:49 PM||||try putting a tennis ball in your exhaust. It will be quiet until the exhaust gets to the end then you just take the tennis ball out and turn the car off.  It gets quite tiring when you go on long trips but it keeps it quiet!!!!!!!!!<P>(ps....dont actually do this)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bruce||04-08-2000||11:48 PM||||From what I've read, there are two Flowmaster mufflers that fit the Fiero: the "80" series that's used on the 82-92 Firebird, and the "40" series Delta Flow. Are they annoying loud, or "powerfully" loud, and is one quieter than the other. <BR>Thanks,<BR>bb||||reg||1
